* Grendel eggs hatch either sex, standard or Bony (openc2e Creatures 2
* project, our own scripts). Run by openc2e after the world loads (Additions
* folder); safe to repeat.
*
* Grendels come from two kinds of egg, and both always hatched a male from
* the game's own grendel genome ("gren"):
* - the egg pile (2 5 4, up to 20 by x 7020), whose keeper (2 1 52) starts an
*   egg hatching when there are no grendels;
* - the egg machine by the volcano (2 1 25), which lays a grendel egg (2 5 3,
*   genome and sex in its ov00 and ov01) when there are ettins already, and
*   an ettin egg when there are none.
* The owner asked (2026-11-10) for grendel eggs to hatch, at random, a male
* or female, standard or Bony grendel (the Boney Grendels pack's genome
* "bone", from the player's own Genetics folder; the pack's mating script,
* the Bony Grendel Update, is built in through builtin-cobs.txt). These two
* hatching scripts replace the eggs' own timer scripts; the keeper and the
* machine are unchanged. Ettin eggs (also from the machine) hatch a male or
* female at random too (owner, 2026-11-10; they were always male).
* C1 grendels joined them (owner, 2026-11-27): a third each of C2's own,
* Boney and C1 ("c1gr", made by the engine when the C1-in-C2 Grendel
* pictures are installed; Kinds.h).
*
* The egg pile's egg: pictures 0-2 while it waits (each step a random 3-6 s
* apart once started), 3-9 cracking, 10 the empty shell, gone at 11.
scrp 2 5 4 9
  doif pose ge 10
    doif pose eq 11 kill ownr stop endi
    pose 11 tick 200 stop
  endi
  doif pose lt 3
    setv var0 pose addv var0 1 pose var0
    rndv var0 30 60 tick var0 stop
  endi
  tick 0
* (the world's limit, which counts every creature: wait while it is full,
* as the game's norn eggs do; EGGL is the limit less the grendels and ettins
* alive, so this compares all creatures with it; owner, 2026-11-16)
  doif totl 4 1 0 ge eggl tick 1200 stop endi
* (one grendel at a time from the pile, as its keeper means: with a grendel
* alive, or another of the pile's eggs hatching (OV02 1), it goes back to
* the pile to wait for the keeper. Eggs the keeper had started while the
* world was full waited in step and hatched together when room opened:
* twelve grendels at once in Home; owner, 2026-11-24. INST: all in one go,
* or each egg's look at the others is cut short, and every egg looks
* before any marks itself)
  inst
  setv ov02 0
  setv var0 0
  enum 2 5 4 doif ov02 eq 1 addv var0 1 endi next
  targ ownr
* (owner, 2026-11-26: as many grendels from the pile as Preferences > World
* says, one unless set: GRNL; with that many alive, counting eggs already
* hatching, it waits)
  setv var1 totl 4 2 0 addv var1 var0
  doif var1 ge grnl pose 0 stop endi
  setv ov02 1
  slow
* (the hatching cannot be cut off: a creature pushing, pulling or hitting
* the egg runs the world's catch-all object script, 2 0 0 1-3, on it, which
* ended this script mid-hatch with the timer stopped, and the egg never
* hatched; 2026-11-19. A retry timer, too, in case it is ever cut off.)
  lock tick 300
* (a third of each: C2's own, Boney and C1 grendels; owner, 2026-11-27.
* A missing pack's genome gives C2's own: NEW: GENE.)
  rndv var0 0 2
  doif var0 eq 0 new: gene tokn gren tokn gren var4 endi
  doif var0 eq 1 new: gene tokn bone tokn bone var4 endi
  doif var0 eq 2 new: gene tokn c1gr tokn c1gr var4 endi
  rndv var3 1 2
  snde crak
  anim [34563456345634563456] over
  wait 20
  anim [3456778899] over
* (the baby stands where the egg lay: its feet at the egg's bottom. The
* game's eggs set its top at the egg's middle, its feet some 30 px under
* the floor, in the room below; 2026-11-18)
  setv var0 posl setv var1 posb
  inst new: crea var4 var3 drea 1 setv var2 posb subv var2 post subv var1 var2 mvto var0 var1 slim setv grav 1
  targ ownr pose 10 tick 200
endm
*
* The egg pile's keeper (C2's own timer, otherwise as it was): it starts one
* of the pile's eggs hatching while fewer grendels live than Preferences >
* World says (GRNL, one unless set; C2's: none alive), now and then stops
* one at exactly that many, and keeps the pile topped up to 20.
scrp 2 1 52 9
  targ ownr tick 1000
  setv var0 totl 4 2 0
  doif var0 lt grnl
    rtar 2 5 4 doif targ ne 0 tick 200 endi
  else
    doif var0 eq grnl
      rndv var1 0 9 doif var1 eq 0 rtar 2 5 4 doif targ ne 0 tick 0 endi endi
    endi
  endi
  setv var0 totl 2 5 4
  doif var0 lt 20
    inst setv var0 7020 setv var1 1280 new: simp greg 12 0 2 0 setv cls2 2 5 4 setv attr 192 rndv var3 0 2 pose var3 rndv var2 -30 30 addv var2 var0 mvto var2 var1 slim setv grav 1 slow
  endi
endm
*
* The egg machine's egg: pictures 3-6 rocking and cracking, 7 the empty
* shell. A grendel egg is made a Bony one a third of the time and a C1 one
* a third; grendel and ettin eggs alike hatch either sex. The machine's
* eggs have OV01 1 (the gene splicer's eggs, of the same class, leave it 0),
* and it lays a grendel egg only while there are ettins (with none, an ettin
* egg). OV00 can't tell them apart: since NEW: GENE works (2026-11-12) it
* holds each egg's own new genome, not "gren" or "ettn".
scrp 2 5 3 9
  tick 0
  doif pose eq 7 kill ownr stop endi
* (the world's limit, as the grendel eggs above)
  doif totl 4 1 0 ge eggl tick 1200 stop endi
* (not to be cut off, and retried if it ever is, as the egg pile's eggs
* above: 13 of the machine's 22 eggs in Home lay at its chute with their
* hatching cut off, some since 2026-11-08)
  lock tick 300
  doif ov01 eq 1
    setv var0 0 enum 4 3 0 addv var0 1 next
    doif var0 gt 0
      rndv var0 0 2
      doif var0 eq 1 new: gene tokn bone tokn bone ov00 endi
      doif var0 eq 2 new: gene tokn c1gr tokn c1gr ov00 endi
    endi
  endi
  rndv var0 1 2 setv ov01 var0
  anim [3456543R] wait 50
  snde crak
  anim [345634563456] over
  pose 7
  setv var1 posx setv var2 posb
  inst new: crea ov00 ov01 drea 1 setv var3 posb subv var3 post subv var2 var3 mvto var1 var2 slim setv grav 1
  targ ownr tick 200
endm
*
* The egg machine lays one egg at a time (owner, 2026-11-20: "Lay one,
* clear extras"). Its timer (C2's own, below as it was) lays an ettin egg
* whenever no ettin lives; an egg hatches only while the norns are under
* the world's limit, so with Home at its limit no ettin came and the
* machine laid on: 74 eggs on one spot at its chute (6308, 2186). Now it
* lays only while none of its eggs (OV01 1) waits. (Its grendel
* subroutine is never called, in C2 as here.)
scrp 2 1 25 9
  setv var1 0
  enum 2 5 3
    doif ov01 eq 1 addv var1 1 endi
  next
  doif var1 gt 0 stop endi
* (an ettin egg while fewer ettins live than Preferences > World says, one
* unless set: ETNL; owner, 2026-11-26)
  setv var0 0 enum 4 3 0 addv var0 1 next doif var0 lt etnl rtar 3 10 7 mesg writ targ 0 wait 10 gsub ettn stop endi
  subr gren inst rndv var0 0 5 mulv var0 8 new: simp eggs 8 var0 2 0 setv cls2 2 5 3 setv attr 196 bhvr 1 0 new: gene tokn gren tokn gren ov00 setv ov01 1 pose 3 mvto 6308 2090 slim setv grav 1 tick 50 slow retn
  subr ettn inst rndv var0 0 5 mulv var0 8 new: simp eggs 8 var0 2 0 setv cls2 2 5 3 setv attr 196 bhvr 1 0 new: gene tokn ettn tokn ettn ov00 setv ov01 1 pose 3 mvto 6308 2090 slim setv grav 1 tick 50 slow retn
endm
* The pile it left: of its eggs waiting unhatched at the chute (OV01 1,
* picture 3, at x 6308), one is kept and the rest cleared away (73 in
* Home). The gene splicer's eggs (OV01 0, at 6300 and 6310) are not
* touched.
setv var0 0
enum 2 5 3
  doif ov01 eq 1 and pose eq 3 and posl eq 6308
    addv var0 1
    doif var0 gt 1 kill targ endi
  endi
next
*
* Eggs whose hatching was cut off before the scripts above were locked
* (2026-11-19) wait with their timers stopped: start them again at load.
* An empty shell (picture 7) is cleared away; the egg pile's eggs (2 5 4)
* wait with no timer until the pile's keeper starts one, so those that
* were cut off mid-hatch (pictures 3-9) are started again, and the rest
* left to the keeper.
enum 2 5 3
  doif pose eq 7 tick 200 else tick 100 endi
next
enum 2 5 4
  doif pose ge 3 doif pose lt 10 tick 100 endi endi
next
